# Taxonomy.def
# ============
# From your own structure, a Taxonomy tree is compiled to produce your various
# cryptographic and perceptual path hashes (`lib/hash/d/README.md`).

Taxonomy {
  0. author        : EntityID / LegalOrPseudonymousName
  1. publisher     : EntityID
  2. distributor   : DistributionChannel
  3. localiser     : LocaleCode
  4. regional      : RegionCode
  5. rational      : CreationIntent / WorkClassification
  6. national      : ISO-3166-1 Jurisdiction
  8. international : TreatyFramework (e.g. Berne-Convention-1886, WIPO-WPPT)
  9. industry      : IndustryTaxonomy (e.g. Audio/Master-Recording, Stem/MIDI)
  10. legal        : LegalProvisions (see d/legal/Legal.def — AI training opt-out & reservation)
  11. unique       : PerceptualSpectralHash256 + StemMerkleRoot
  12. crypto_proof : CleanMasterSHA256 + ProtectedMasterSHA256 + OpenTimestampsProof
  13. universe_loc : UniversalLocationVector (see lib/universe/d/location.def)
}
